wm-darwin autopilot: a Touch Bar phase

Phase `touchbar`, after `volume`: finger records for F11, F11, F12, F12, F10, F10 and
Escape are written to the Touch Bar driver's test entry (kern.sf_touchbar.inject, in the
digitizer's units, at the positions kern.sf_touchbar.keys gives). The driver parses them
as it parses the digitizer's reports; the keys come back through IOHIDFamily and the
SFHID device node like any key. The phase counts the key events delivered (two per touch,
Escape's release last) and, with an audio server, reads its level back after each of the
six volume touches as the volume phase does. Without the driver it reports SKIPPED.
Server::hid_keys() counts delivered key events for it.

Applies on top of the uncommitted volume-key change (../m1-sound/sysaudio/
wm-darwin-volume-keys.commit) in sources/chonkstep-darwin, branch wm-darwin, commit
d92ac89; working tree only, not committed there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
